Felix Lee (flee@cs.psu.edu) wrote:
: I always wonder, what sort of game are people thinking about when they
: say they want a multiplayer form of nethack?
: 
: I suspect what people want is sort of a hybrid between MUDs and
: multiplayer arcade games.  The MUDs aren't sufficiently spatial;
: arcade games don't have enough nouns and verbs.

Oh, MUDs are lots of fun, believe me... :-)
Nethack wouldn't fit to the multiplayer form without some heavy modification
to the main plot. I can imagine having 10 players in the Wizard's room at the
same time, shouting "I was here first! He's mine!". Also, the artifacts are
another problem. Anyway, I'd love this kind of game. Players could form groups
to kick the heck out of those hill orc hordes, do stuff like "you go left,
we'll get the right side" etc. Groups probably should agree with some basic
battle strategies to let the mage blast the nasties with area-effect spells
and to let archers shoot from far away. Communication during battle isn't so
easy with a keyboard.
 So, lots could be done with a Nethack-style interface. Basically I'd want a
game with lots of action and some special quests, much like NH. There should
probably be a bit more variety to avoid boredom. Then again, I'm still not
bored with NH... what am I talking about?

